note right of p8080 #FFE4E6
  **The single highest-severity fact in this audit.**
  `auth.py:17-20` states the no-auth design is
  "NOT fine if the port is published to a network you
  do not control — see the compose port bindings."
  The compose port binding is `"8080:8080"`, which
  Docker binds to **0.0.0.0**, not 127.0.0.1.
  The precondition the code relies on is not met.

  Fix (one line per service):
  `- "127.0.0.1:8080:8080"`
end note

note right of intns #F0FDF4
  Done correctly: SearXNG has **no** host port and
  is reachable only as `http://searxng:8080` from
  the orchestrator (docker-compose.yml:333-344).
  This is the pattern the vLLM services should follow.
end note

note bottom of webe #FFFBEB
  All user-influenced outbound fetches funnel through
  ONE choke point, `core/net.py:103 safe_fetch()`:
  DNS resolved and checked before connect, every
  redirect hop re-validated, body + time capped.
  Residual gap: resolve-then-connect is a TOCTOU
  window (see SEC-03).
end note

legend right
  |= Colour |= Meaning |
  |<#FECACA> | published **and** unauthenticated |
  |<#DBEAFE> | published, UI surface |
  |<#DCFCE7> | internal only — not reachable off-host |
  |<#E2E8F0> | outbound egress |
  Solid red = unauthenticated inbound path.
  Ports written `host:container`.
end legend

